<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antoine III de Gramont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1604">1604</a>–<a href="/years/1678">1678</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Antoine III, Duke of Gramont</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antoine III de Gramont was a French noble, sovereign lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidache">Bidache</a> and Marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1641. He served as a commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War and as a diplomat under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>, negotiating the king's marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. He was created duke of Gramont in 1643.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoine-iii-de-gramont.jpg" alt="Antoine III de Gramont" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antoine_III_de_Gramont_-_Basque_Museum_in_Bayonne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
